{"abstract":"Pomelo fruit is naturally rich in health-promoting components. However, few studies have quantified phytic acid (PA), which is both an antioxidant compound and an antinutrient that limits mineral bioavailability. In this study, we analyzed the temporospatial changes in fruit PA, total phenolic, total flavonoid, estimated mineral bioavailabilities, and their response to fertilization strategies. Compared to pulp, pomelo peel contained higher PA, total phenolic, total flavonoid and most minerals concentrations (except for P) but lower estimated mineral bioavailabilities (Mg, Zn and Fe). The concentrations of PA, total flavonoid, and minerals (P, Ca, Mg, Zn) and Fe estimated bioavailability in pulp gradually decreased with ripening. Total phenolic concentrations and the estimated bioavailabilities of Ca, Mg and Zn in pulp decreased in the early fruit expansion stage but subsequently increased markedly until maturity. Reduced chemical fertilization while supplementing Mg simultaneously increased estimated mineral bioavailabilities in pulp through reduced PA as an antinutrient, and increased bioactives concentrations in peel through increased PA as an antioxidant together with total phenolic and total flavonoid. Overall, our results indicate that reducing NPK while supplementing Mg fertilization in pomelo orchards with acidic and Mg-deficient soil is the most beneficial approach for achieving biofortification of the edible pulp parts and integrated fruit quality enhancement.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Su, Da","Song, Biao","Wu, Hongyu","Chen, Xiaohui","Zhang, Jiangzhou","Rasmussen, Søren Kjærsgaard","Wu, Liangquan","Ye, Delian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720302"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anhui Agricultural University","Fujian Agriculture and Forestry University"],"keyword":["Bioactive compound","Faculty of Science","Fertilization","Phytic acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variations in phytic acid phenolic flavonoid and mineral bioavailabilities during pomelo fruit development and their relation to fertilization strategy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-720302","identifier":[{"id":"85180575125","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-56f03c01-1b1c-445a-ae7d-d0e0518c3503"],"keyword":["Bioactive compound","Faculty of Science","Fertilization","Mineral bioavailability","Phytic acid","Pomelo"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E62E517545FF42F2DD811C0A6A475E4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"fujian agriculture and forestry university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Fujian Agriculture and Forestry University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"anhui agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Anhui Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant and Soil Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Da","key":"sudapau","last":"Su","name":"Su, Da","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Biao","key":"songbiaopau","last":"Song","name":"Song, Biao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hongyu","key":"wuhongyupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Hongyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Xiaohui","key":"chenxiaohuipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xiaohui","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jiangzhou","key":"zhangjiangzhoupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Jiangzhou","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Søren K.","key":"rasmussensørenkjærsgaardpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"95b8db6a-2621-49dc-bf1f-dbba5884b8da","name":"Rasmussen, Søren Kjærsgaard","name_org":"Rasmussen, Søren K.","orcid":"0000-0001-6169-2504","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Liangquan","key":"wuliangquanpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Liangquan","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Delian","key":"yedelianpau","last":"Ye","name":"Ye, Delian","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scienta.2023.112804","issn":["03044238"],"journal":"Scientia Horticulturae","paperid":"112804","status":"p","title":"Scientia Horticulturae","volume":"327"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180575125"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-56f03c01-1b1c-445a-ae7d-d0e0518c3503"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Variations in phytic acid, phenolic, flavonoid, and mineral-bioavailabilities during pomelo fruit development and their relation to fertilization strategy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720302","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The increasing penetration of renewables in power systems reconfigures the generation mix and geography distribution, resulting in more frequent power flow congestion. Conventionally, a relatively conservative dispatch margin for transmission congestion in network constraints was reserved to ensure safe operation due to potential deviations introduced by DC power flow modeling and conservative line rating. This paper proposes a real-time power market clearing model with improved network constraints considering power transfer distribution factor (PTDF) correction and fast-calculated dynamic line rating. The clearing model based on PTDF correction is proposed first employing the Taylor expansion with the voltage and phase angle approximation. An improved dynamic line rating model is further applied into the clearing model based on the piecewise linear approximation method, which calculates real-time conductor temperature faster with sufficient precision. We test and verify the validity of the proposed model based on three independent systems including the IEEE 39-bus system, the IEEE 2383-bus system, and the real power grid system in Yunnan province of China, respectively. The results show that the improved clearing model reduces the calculated power flow deviation between the clearing results and real conditions compared with traditional security constraints, where the efficiency of power grid operation is also increased.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pan, Hongyu","Chen, Xinyu","Jin, Tianyu","Bai, Yang","Chen, Zhongfei","Wen, Jinyu","Wu, Qiuwei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-669355"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","China Southern Power Grid","Huazhong University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Adaptation models","Load flow","Mathematical models","Power grids","Power system dynamics","Real time systems","Taylor series"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real time power market clearing model with improved network constraints considering ptdf correction and fast calculated dynamic line rating","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/297228107/hkkr_Real_Time_Power_Market_Clearing_Model_with_Improved_Network_Constraints_Considering_PTDF_Correction_and_Fast_Calculated_Dynamic_Line_Rating.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-669355","identifier":[{"id":"85141631684","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-94cd8f06-381b-423e-ab2c-47508d31a9d7"],"keyword":["Adaptation models","Load flow","Mathematical models","Power grids","Power system dynamics","Real-time systems","Taylor series"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78E2929CA329811916D30BAB859B4208"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/297228107/hkkr_Real_Time_Power_Market_Clearing_Model_with_Improved_Network_Constraints_Considering_PTDF_Correction_and_Fast_Calculated_Dynamic_Line_Rating.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"huazhong university of science and technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Huazhong University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"china southern power grid","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"China Southern Power Grid","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"panhongyupau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Hongyu","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xinyu","key":"chenxinyupau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xinyu","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tianyu","key":"jintianyupau","last":"Jin","name":"Jin, Tianyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yang","key":"baiyangpau","last":"Bai","name":"Bai, Yang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhongfei","key":"chenzhongfeipau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Zhongfei","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinyu","key":"wenjinyupau","last":"Wen","name":"Wen, Jinyu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qiuwei","key":"wuqiuweipau","last":"Wu","locid":"271c52b0-febb-4f56-8609-f2cb7b98a801","name":"Wu, Qiuwei","orcid":"0000-0001-7935-2567","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tia.2022.3218271","issn":["00939994"],"issn_org":["19399367"],"issue":"2","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Industry Applications","pages":"2130-2139","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Industry Applications","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141631684"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-94cd8f06-381b-423e-ab2c-47508d31a9d7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Real-Time Power Market Clearing Model with Improved Network Constraints Considering PTDF Correction and Fast-Calculated Dynamic Line Rating","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-669355","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Transition metal oxides with high capacity still confront the challenges of low initial coulombic efficiency (ICE, generally <70%) and inferior cyclic stability for practical lithium-storage. Herein, a hollow slender carambola-like Li0.43FeO1.51 with Fe vacancies is proposed by a facile reaction of Fe3+-containing metal–organic frameworks with Li2CO3. Synthesis experiments combined with synchrotron-radiation X-ray measurements identify that the hollow structure is caused by Li2CO3 erosion, while the formation of Fe vacancies is resulted from insufficient lithiation process with reduced Li2CO3 dosage. The optimized lithium iron oxides exhibit remarkably improved ICE (from 68.24% to 86.78%), high-rate performance (357 mAh g−1 at 5 A g−1), and superior cycling stability (884 mAh g−1 after 500 cycles at 0.5 A g−1). Paring with LiFePO4 cathodes, the full-cells achieve extraordinary cyclic stability with 99.3% retention after 100 cycles. The improved electrochemical performances can be attributed to the synergy of structural characteristics and Fe vacancy engineering. The unique hollow structure alleviates the volume expansion of Li0.43FeO1.51, while the in situ generated Fe vacancies are powerful for modulating electronic structure with boosted Li+ transport rate and catalyze more Li2O decomposition to react with Fe in the first charge process, hence enhancing the ICE of lithium iron oxide anode materials.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Wu, Naiteng","Shen, Jinke","Yong, Kai","Chen, Chengqian","Li, Jian","Xie, Yi","Guo, Donglei","Liu, Guilong","Li, Jin","Cao, Ang","Liu, Xianming","Mi, Hongyu","Wu, Hao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695052"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Xianming","Mi, Hongyu","Wu, Hao"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luoyang Normal University","Sichuan University","Xinjiang University"],"keyword":["Electronic structure modulation","Lithium ion batteries"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synergistic structure and iron vacancy engineering realizing high initial coulombic efficiency and kinetically accelerated lithium storage in lithium iron oxide","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202206574","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["N.W., J.S., and K.Y. contributed equally to this work. The authors acknowledge the financial support from the Natural Science Foundations of China [Nos. 51904152 and 21965033], Natural Science Foundations of Henan Province [No. 222300420502], the Program for Science and Technology Innovation Talents in Universities of Henan Province [No. 20HASTIT020], and the Key Science and Technology Program of Henan Province [No. 222102240044]."],"id":"S01-000.00-695052","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10037985","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85146683695","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36683228","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-9fd38bb5-6bdb-4b96-8039-2343898dbaaa"],"keyword":["Electronic structure modulation","High initial coulombic efficiency","Iron vacancies","Lithium iron oxide","Lithium-ion batteries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E410E84995B48A0ED7596527913EF588"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/314464494/Advanced_Science_2023_Wu_Synergistic_Structure_and_Iron_Vacancy_Engineering_Realizing_High_Initial_Coulombic.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/advs.202206574","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"luoyang normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Luoyang Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"xinjiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xinjiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"sichuan university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Catalysis Theory Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Naiteng","key":"wunaitengpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Naiteng","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jinke","key":"shenjinkepau","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, Jinke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kai","key":"yongkaipau","last":"Yong","name":"Yong, Kai","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chengqian","key":"chenchengqianpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Chengqian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"lijianpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yi","key":"xieyipau","last":"Xie","name":"Xie, Yi","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Donglei","key":"guodongleipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Donglei","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guilong","key":"liuguilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guilong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin","key":"lijinpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Jin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ang","key":"caoangpau","last":"Cao","locid":"bcb0a893-26f0-4e9c-84d6-ec895a5d3a7b","name":"Cao, Ang","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianming","key":"liuxianmingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xianming","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"mihongyupau","last":"Mi","name":"Mi, Hongyu","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao","key":"wuhaopau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Hao","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36683228"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/advs.202206574","issn":["21983844"],"issue":"9","journal":"Advanced Science","paperid":"2206574","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Advanced Science","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146683695"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9fd38bb5-6bdb-4b96-8039-2343898dbaaa"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Synergistic Structure and Iron-Vacancy Engineering Realizing High Initial Coulombic Efficiency and Kinetically Accelerated Lithium Storage in Lithium Iron Oxide","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695052","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The electronic structure regulation of electrode materials can improve the ion/electron kinetics, which is beneficial to the cyclic performance and rate capability for lithium ion batteries (LIBs). Herein, we propose a facile strategy to achieve a MoO2/Mo2C/C heterostructure with abundant oxygen vacancies. Density functional theory calculations indicate that the heterostructure of MoO2/Mo2C/C can significantly promote the Li+/charge transfer and reduce the Li adsorption energy, and the abundant oxygen vacancies in MoO2/Mo2C/C can improve the intrinsic electronic conductivity and reduce the Li+ diffusion barrier. Benefiting from the multiscale coordinated regulation, the obtained MoO2/Mo2C/C film exhibits outstanding high rate capability (454.7 mA h g−1 at 5 A g−1) and remarkable cyclic performance (retaining 569 mA h g−1 over 1000 cycles at 2 A g−1). The insightful findings in this study can shed light on the behavior of the electron/ion structure regulation by the heterostructure and oxygen vacancies, which can guide future studies on designing other electrode materials with high-performance lithium-ion storage.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Guo, Donglei","Yang, Mengke","Wang, Fang","Cheng, Yihua","Zhang, Anqi","Liu, Guilong","Wu, Naiteng","Cao, Ang","Mi, Hongyu","Liu, Xianming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-358561"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Xianming","Mi, Hongyu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luoyang Normal University","Xinjiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regulating the electronic structure of moo sub 000000000002 sub mo sub 000000000002 sub c c by heterostructure and oxygen vacancies for boosting lithium storage kinetics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85135584795","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-358561","identifier":[{"id":"85135584795","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000837446800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"35925026","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-b4ba3800-7eb9-4c8f-9f6f-9a7e634586d5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E524E4A2812C97C031F171CCB6D1B6F2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"luoyang normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Luoyang Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Catalysis Theory Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"xinjiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xinjiang University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Donglei","key":"guodongleipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Donglei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mengke","key":"yangmengkepau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Mengke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fang","key":"wangfangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Fang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yihua","key":"chengyihuapau","last":"Cheng","name":"Cheng, Yihua","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anqi","key":"zhanganqipau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Anqi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guilong","key":"liuguilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guilong","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Naiteng","key":"wunaitengpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Naiteng","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ang","key":"caoangpau","last":"Cao","locid":"bcb0a893-26f0-4e9c-84d6-ec895a5d3a7b","name":"Cao, Ang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"mihongyupau","last":"Mi","name":"Mi, Hongyu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianming","key":"liuxianmingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xianming","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35925026"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d2dt01917e","issn":["14779226","14779234"],"issn_org":["14779226"],"journal":"Dalton Transactions","pages":"12620-12629","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Dalton Transactions","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135584795"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b4ba3800-7eb9-4c8f-9f6f-9a7e634586d5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Regulating the electronic structure of MoO<sub>2</sub>/Mo<sub>2</sub>C/C by heterostructure and oxygen vacancies for boosting lithium storage kinetics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-358561","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Regulating the electronic structure plays a positive role in improving the ion/electron kinetics of electrode materials for lithium ion batteries (LIBs). Herein, an effective approach is demonstrated to achieve Ni/Mo2C hybrid nanoparticles embedded in porous nitrogen-doped carbon nanofibers (Ni/Mo2C/NC). Density functional theory calculations indicate that Ni can activate the interface of Ni/Mo2C by regulating the electronic structure, and accordingly improve the electron/Li-ion diffusion kinetics. The charge at the interface transfers from Ni atoms to Mo atoms on the surface of Mo2C, illustrating the formation of an interfacial electric field in Ni/Mo2C. The formed interfacial electric field in Ni/Mo2C can improve the intrinsic electronic conductivity, and reduce the Li adsorption energy and the Li+ diffusion barrier. Thus, the obtained Ni/Mo2C/NC shows an excellent high-rate capability of 344.1 mA h g−1 at 10 A g−1, and also displays a superior cyclic performance (remaining at 412.7 mA h g−1 after 1800 cycles at 2 A g−1). This work demonstrates the important role of electronic structure regulation by assembling hybrid materials and provides new guidance for future work on designing novel electrode materials for LIBs.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Guo, Donglei","Yang, Mengke","Xu, Shu","Zhu, Shuping","Liu, Guilong","Wu, Naiteng","Cao, Ang","Mi, Hongyu","Liu, Xianming"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-368557"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, Xianming","Mi, Hongyu"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Luoyang Normal University","Xinjiang University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ni activated mo sub 000000000002 sub c by regulating the interfacial electronic structure for highly efficient lithium ion storage","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140144321","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the National Natural Science Foundation of China (grant number 51904152); the Key Science and Technology Program of Henan Province (grant number 222102240044); the Program for Science & Technology Innovation Talents in Universities of Henan Province (grant number 20HASTIT020) and the Natural Science Foundations of Henan Province (grant number 222300420502)."],"id":"S01-000.00-368557","identifier":[{"id":"36149683","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85140144321","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d62f066e-4ab6-48d9-966e-b8adc9aa0f7e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0AAF36AFFB3E798F33A190155F7FB83F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"luoyang normal university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Luoyang Normal University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Catalysis Theory Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"xinjiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Xinjiang University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Donglei","key":"guodongleipau","last":"Guo","name":"Guo, Donglei","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mengke","key":"yangmengkepau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Mengke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shu","key":"xushupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Shu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shuping","key":"zhushupingpau","last":"Zhu","name":"Zhu, Shuping","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guilong","key":"liuguilongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Guilong","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Naiteng","key":"wunaitengpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Naiteng","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ang","key":"caoangpau","last":"Cao","locid":"bcb0a893-26f0-4e9c-84d6-ec895a5d3a7b","name":"Cao, Ang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"mihongyupau","last":"Mi","name":"Mi, Hongyu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianming","key":"liuxianmingpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Xianming","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36149683"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/d2nr03832c","issn":["20403364","20403372"],"issn_org":["20403364"],"issue":"39","journal":"Nanoscale","pages":"14575-14584","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Nanoscale","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140144321"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d62f066e-4ab6-48d9-966e-b8adc9aa0f7e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Ni activated Mo<sub>2</sub>C by regulating the interfacial electronic structure for highly efficient lithium-ion storage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-368557","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Posttraumatic stress disorder (PTSD) is heritable and a potential consequence of exposure to traumatic stress. Evidence suggests that a quantitative approach to PTSD phenotype measurement and incorporation of lifetime trauma exposure (LTE) information could enhance the discovery power of PTSD genome-wide association studies (GWASs). Methods: A GWAS on PTSD symptoms was performed in 51 cohorts followed by a fixed-effects meta-analysis (N = 182,199 European ancestry participants). A GWAS of LTE burden was performed in the UK Biobank cohort (N = 132,988). Genetic correlations were evaluated with linkage disequilibrium score regression. Multivariate analysis was performed using Multi-Trait Analysis of GWAS. Functional mapping and annotation of leading loci was performed with FUMA. Replication was evaluated using the Million Veteran Program GWAS of PTSD total symptoms. Results: GWASs of PTSD symptoms and LTE burden identified 5 and 6 independent genome-wide significant loci, respectively. There was a 72% genetic correlation between PTSD and LTE. PTSD and LTE showed largely similar patterns of genetic correlation with other traits, albeit with some distinctions. Adjusting PTSD for LTE reduced PTSD heritability by 31%. Multivariate analysis of PTSD and LTE increased the effective sample size of the PTSD GWAS by 20% and identified 4 additional loci. Four of these 9 PTSD loci were independently replicated in the Million Veteran Program. Conclusions: Through using a quantitative trait measure of PTSD, we identified novel risk loci not previously identified using prior case-control analyses. PTSD and LTE have a high genetic overlap that can be leveraged to increase discovery power through multivariate methods.","author_count":196,"contributors":["Maihofer, Adam X.","Choi, Karmel W.","Coleman, Jonathan R.I.","Daskalakis, Nikolaos P.","Denckla, Christy A.","Ketema, Elizabeth","Morey, Rajendra A.","Polimanti, Renato","Ratanatharathorn, Andrew","Torres, Katy","Wingo, Aliza P.","Zai, Clement C.","Aiello, Allison E.","Almli, Lynn M.","Amstadter, Ananda B.","Andersen, Soren B.","Andreassen, Ole A.","Arbisi, Paul A.","Ashley-Koch, Allison E.","Austin, S. Bryn","Avdibegović, Esmina","Børglum, Anders D","Babić, Dragan","Bækvad-Hansen, Marie","Baker, Dewleen G.","Beckham, Jean C.","Bierut, Laura J.","Bisson, Jonathan I.","Boks, Marco P.","Bolger, Elizabeth A.","Bradley, Bekh","Brashear, Meghan","Breen, Gerome","Bryant, Richard A.","Bustamante, Angela C.","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Calabrese, Joseph R.","Caldas-de-Almeida, José M.","Chen, Chia Yen","Dale, Anders M.","Dalvie, Shareefa","Deckert, Jürgen","Delahanty, Douglas L.","Dennis, Michelle F.","Disner, Seth G.","Domschke, Katharina","Duncan, Laramie E.","Džubur Kulenović, Alma","Erbes, Christopher R.","Evans, Alexandra","Farrer, Lindsay A.","Feeny, Norah C.","Flory, Janine D.","Forbes, David","Franz, Carol E.","Galea, Sandro","Garrett, Melanie E.","Gautam, Aarti","Gelaye, Bizu","Gelernter, Joel","Geuze, Elbert","Gillespie, Charles F.","Goçi, Aferdita","Gordon, Scott D.","Guffanti, Guia","Hammamieh, Rasha","Hauser, Michael A.","Heath, Andrew C.","Hemmings, Sian M.J.","Hougaard, David Michael","Jakovljević, Miro","Jett, Marti","Johnson, Eric Otto","Jones, Ian","Jovanovic, Tanja","Qin, Xue Jun","Karstoft, Karen Inge","Kaufman, Milissa L.","Kessler, Ronald C.","Khan, Alaptagin","Kimbrel, Nathan A.","King, Anthony P.","Koen, Nastassja","Kranzler, Henry R.","Kremen, William S.","Lawford, Bruce R.","Lebois, Lauren A.M.","Lewis, Catrin","Liberzon, Israel","Linnstaedt, Sarah D.","Logue, Mark W.","Lori, Adriana","Lugonja, Božo","Luykx, Jurjen J.","Lyons, Michael J.","Maples-Keller, Jessica L.","Marmar, Charles","Martin, Nicholas G.","Maurer, Douglas","Mavissakalian, Matig R.","McFarlane, Alexander","McGlinchey, Regina E.","McLaughlin, Katie A.","McLean, Samuel A.","Mehta, Divya","Mellor, Rebecca","Michopoulos, Vasiliki","Milberg, William","Miller, Mark W.","Morris, Charles Phillip