I:S02-091.30-030714","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Panicle degeneration, sometimes known as abortion, causes heavy losses in grain yield. However, the mechanism of naturally occurring panicle abortion is still elusive. In a previous study, we characterized a mutant, apical panicle abortion1331 (apa1331), exhibiting abortion in apical spikelets starting from the 6 cm stage of panicle development. In this study, we have quantified the five phytohormones, gibberellins (GA), auxins (IAA), abscisic acid (ABA), cytokinins (CTK), and brassinosteroids (BR), in the lower, middle, and upper parts of apa1331 and compared these with those exhibited in its wild type (WT). In apa331, the lower and middle parts of the panicle showed contrasting concentrations of all studied phytohormones, but highly significant changes in IAA and ABA, compared to the upper part of the panicle. A comparative transcriptome of apa1331 and WT apical spikelets was performed to explore genes causing the physiological basis of spikelet abortion. The differential expression analysis revealed a significant downregulation and upregulation of 1587 and 978 genes, respectively. Hierarchical clustering of differentially expressed genes (DEGs) revealed the correlation of gene ontology (GO) terms associated with antioxidant activity, peroxidase activity, and oxidoreductase activity. KEGG pathway analysis using parametric gene set enrichment analysis (PGSEA) revealed the downregulation of the biological processes, including cell wall polysaccharides and fatty acids derivatives, in apa1331 compared to its WT. Based on fold change (FC) value and high variation in expression during late inflorescence, early inflorescence, and antherdevelopment, we predicted a list of novel genes, which presumably can be the potential targets of inflorescence development. Our study not only provides novel insights into the role of the physiological dynamics involved in panicle abortion, but also highlights the potential targets involved in reproductive development.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Ali, Asif","Wu, Tingkai","Xu, Zhengjun","Riaz, Asad","Alqudah, Ahmad M.","Iqbal, Muhammad Zafar","Zhang, Hongyu","Liao, Yongxiang","Chen, Xiaoqiong","Liu, Yutong","Mujtaba, Tahir","Zhou, Hao","Wang, Wenming","Xu, Peizhou","Wu, Xianjun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-268950"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sichuan Agricultural University","University of Verona","Zhejiang University"],"keyword":["DEG","Phytohormone","Transcriptome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"phytohormones and transcriptome analyses revealed the dynamics involved in spikelet abortion and inflorescence development in rice","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms23147887","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-268950","identifier":[{"id":"000832377000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9324563","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35887236","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85135125182","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f4dd41e3-a753-47f4-bff6-473deec5eade"],"keyword":["DEG","inflorescence development","phytohormone","spikelet abortion","transcriptome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2C62194D7DF213278D84E3D264CA86A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms23147887","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"sichuan agricultural university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Sichuan Agricultural University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"zhejiang university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Zhejiang University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Crop Genetics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of verona","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Verona","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asif","key":"aliasifpau","last":"Ali","name":"Ali, Asif","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tingkai","key":"wutingkaipau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Tingkai","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zhengjun","key":"xuzhengjunpau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Zhengjun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Asad","key":"riazasadpau","last":"Riaz","name":"Riaz, Asad","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmad M.","key":"alqudahahmadmpau","last":"Alqudah","locid":"dac730b6-2862-4362-af84-b2d75edf4183","name":"Alqudah, Ahmad M.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Muhammad Zafar","key":"iqbalmuhammadzafarpau","last":"Iqbal","name":"Iqbal, Muhammad Zafar","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"zhanghongyupau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Hongyu","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yongxiang","key":"liaoyongxiangpau","last":"Liao","name":"Liao, Yongxiang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoqiong","key":"chenxiaoqiongpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Xiaoqiong","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yutong","key":"liuyutongpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Yutong","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahir","key":"mujtabatahirpau","last":"Mujtaba","name":"Mujtaba, Tahir","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao","key":"zhouhaopau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Hao","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wenming","key":"wangwenmingpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Wenming","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peizhou","key":"xupeizhoupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Peizhou","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xianjun","key":"wuxianjunpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xianjun","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35887236"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijms23147887","issn":["14220067","16616596"],"issn_org":["16616596"],"issue":"14","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","paperid":"7887","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135125182"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f4dd41e3-a753-47f4-bff6-473deec5eade"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Phytohormones and Transcriptome Analyses Revealed the Dynamics Involved in Spikelet Abortion and Inflorescence Development in Rice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-268950","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Strengthening the physical and chemical interaction between the metal and support of metal-based catalysts is one of the most effective ways to enhance their catalytic performance in heterogeneous organic catalysis. Therefore, the catalysts may possess high catalytic performance if they are designed as a confined structure, such as a metal species@support material. However, the encapsulation method usually suffers from a complicated preparation route. In this work, an encapsulated bimetallic catalyst is prepared, and its catalytic performance is evaluated in the hydrogenation of nitroarenes and azo dyes. Specifically, with the developed substrate-assisted encapsulation strategy, bimetallic Pd-Fe nanoparticles are facilely trapped between amine-functionalized silica nanotubes (SNTs) and polydopamine (PDA)-derived N-doped carbon (NC) layers. The resultant SNTs/Pd-Fe/NC bimetallic catalyst exhibits excellent catalytic efficiency toward hydrogenation of nitroarenes and azo dyes due to the unique microstructures. Typically, in catalytic reduction of 4-nitrophenol, the turnover frequency is as high as 401.28 min-1, which is the highest performance among the recently reported noble-metal nanoparticle-based catalysts. Furthermore, the current strategy is beneficial for further design and preparation of active and stable catalysts with broad applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Zhang, Ning","Qiu, Yuan","Sun, Hongyu","Hao, Jufang","Chen, Jun","Xi, Jiangbo","Liu, Jin","He, Baojiang","Bai, Zheng Wu"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-359510"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Xi, Jiangbo"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hubei University","State Tobacco Monopoly Administration, China Tobacco Corporation","Wuhan Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Organocatalysis","Reduction reaction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"substrate assisted encapsulation of pd fe bimetal nanoparticles on functionalized silica nanotubes for catalytic hydrogenation of nitroarenes and azo dyes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85108641404","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was financially supported by the Natural Science Foundation of Hubei Province (nos. 2019CFB539, 2016CFB262, and 2018CFB159), the National Natural Science Foundation of China (nos. 51772110 and 51971055), the Open Project of Key Laboratory of Green Chemical Engineering Process of Ministry of Education (no. GCP20200205), and the Open Project of Ministry-of-Education Key Laboratory for the Green Preparation and Application of Functional Materials. The authors acknowledge Dr. Muhammad Asif for her kind help in polishing the English language of the manuscript."],"id":"S01-000.00-359510","identifier":[{"id":"85108641404","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b7d03d0e-e14a-4b3f-982a-4c00b15e8fd9"],"keyword":["Bimetal catalyst","Encapsulated nanoparticle","Organocatalysis","Reduction reaction","Substrate-assisted method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-984717ACBE64FF4CD36A4D9309C2548D"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"wuhan institute of technology","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Wuhan Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"state tobacco monopoly administration china tobacco corporation","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"State Tobacco Monopoly Administration, China Tobacco Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"cn","key":"hubei university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Hubei University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ning","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Ning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuan","key":"qiupau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, Yuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hongyu","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","locid":"202a2263-7dcc-4eaf-a63d-5a425eb203d8","name":"Sun, Hongyu","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jufang","key":"haopau","last":"Hao","name":"Hao, Jufang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Jun","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jiangbo","key":"xipau","last":"Xi","name":"Xi, Jiangbo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jin","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Jin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Baojiang","key":"hepau","last":"He","name":"He, Baojiang","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zheng Wu","key":"baipau","last":"Bai","name":"Bai, Zheng Wu","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsanm.1c00777","issn":["25740970"],"issue":"6","journal":"ACS Applied Nano Materials","pages":"5854-5863","publisher":"AMER CHEMICAL SOC","status":"p","title":"ACS Applied Nano Materials","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108641404"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b7d03d0e-e14a-4b3f-982a-4c00b15e8fd9"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Substrate-Assisted Encapsulation of Pd-Fe Bimetal Nanoparticles on Functionalized Silica Nanotubes for Catalytic Hydrogenation of Nitroarenes and Azo Dyes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-359510","year":"2021","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Highly ordered ferromagnetic metal nanowire arrays with preferred growth direction show potential applications in electronic and spintronic devices. In this work, by employing a porous anodic aluminum oxide template-assisted electrodeposition method, we successfully prepared Ni nanowire arrays. Importantly, the growth direction of Ni nanowire arrays can be controlled by varying the current densities. The crystalline and growth orientation of Ni nanowire arrays show effects on magnetic properties. Single-crystallinity Ni nanowires with [110] orientation show the best magnetic properties, including coercivity and squareness, along the parallel direction of the nanowire axis. The current preparation strategy can be used to obtain other nanowire arrays (such as metal, alloy, and semiconductor) with controlled growth direction in confined space, and is therefore of broad interest for different applications.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Yu, Yanlong","Li, Jinpeng","Wang, Jun","Wu, Xige","Yu, Cuiyan","Xu, Tao","Chang, Bingdong","Sun, Hongyu","Arandiyan, Hamidreza"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340069"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Sun, Hongyu"],"country":["Australia","China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northeast Petroleum University","Ulvac Research Center Suzhou Co Ltd","University of Sydney"],"keyword":["Electrodeposition","Magnetic properties","Nanowire arrays","Orientation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"orientation growth and magnetic properties of electrochemical deposited nickel nanowire arrays","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/catal9020152","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This research was funded by the National Natural Scientific Foundation of China, grant number 51601037."],"id":"S01-000.00-340069","identifier":[{"id":"85062520536","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-76e8b50a-73b2-427b-a45d-d23f7a87925f"],"keyword":["Electrodeposition","Magnetic properties","Nanowire arrays","Orientation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B6CDDCA8D9943D25B5FB2AA7218209F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/catal9020152","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/169760696/Untitled.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"northeast petroleum university","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Northeast Petroleum University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"ulvac research center suzhou co ltd","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Ulvac Research Center Suzhou Co Ltd","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization","Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization, Nanofabrication","Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization, Nanofabrication, Advanced Nanomachining"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1}],"person":[{"af